<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Vencemos cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Vencemos cut.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Credit Lyonnais Securities said analyst Rafael Diaz had cut his rating for Corporacion Venezolana de Cementos, or Vencemos, to hold from buy.</p>
<p>-- In a Feb 21 report, Diaz wrote he expected the company's operating margin to fall to 32 percent this year from 36 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Although cement prices per metric ton should rise in dollar terms from $80 at year-end 1996 to $85 in 1997 (the increase in bolivar terms would be 15 percent), production costs are expected to increase at the same rate as inflation (36 percent),&quot; he wrote.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
